---
description: Choose the evidence-backed next step without a device effect.
args:
  goal: string
  evidence: PhoneFirstRunEvidence
returns: PhoneFirstRunDecision
budget: { maxTurns: 12 }
---
1. Preserve the original user intent. A pairing from another account or workspace means hold-owner. A rejected process excerpt calls for inspect-native-evidence when the user asks to validate the excerpt or the current readiness is still opening.
2. When the owned visible workspace reports failure or the assigned debug phase parser reports a failure, choose review-startup-failure. A prior connection or shell marker cannot override current failure.
3. For a retained owned pairing, use its exact installed resume status. A ready result can record-ready-evidence within this rehearsal. Opening or unreachable means wait-workspace, including when the native log parser saw both startup markers. Keep the pairing.
4. For unpaired startup diagnosis, choose inspect-native-evidence when a debug excerpt was supplied and the user needs phase readback. Say which phase is still missing. If setup eligibility is requested and no eligible desktop is known, choose open-owned-desktop. If more than one matches, choose choose-desktop.
5. With one exact desktop, keep a compatible existing package with continue-existing-install. Otherwise an authorized review of the source path uses review-source, citing the actual System React Native provider and client ABI. Use review-release for ordinary setup when no compatible release package is installed. Say which evidence supports the next review. None of these recommendations install, pair, or prove a physical device ready.
